To disable hiding of scrollbars in GTK3 applications, source this:

    /etc/profile.d/gtk-classic-themes.sh

If primary paste somehow does not work, do this for your user:

$ gsettings set org.gnome.desktop.interface gtk-enable-primary-paste true

To fix fonts appearance and make scrollbars always visible, create this
file (if it does not exist):

    ~/.config/gtk-4.0/settings.ini

...containing the following:

[Settings]
gtk-hint-font-metrics=true
gtk-font-rendering=manual
gtk-overlay-scrolling=false

By default, Xfce’s desktop cuts the names of unselected icons to one
line with "..." and only shows the full name when you click on the icon.
A GTK style setting turns the cutting off, so every name shows in full,
wrapped over several lines. Add it to your GTK3 user stylesheet, create
this file (if it does not exist):

    ~/.config/gtk-3.0/gtk.css

...containing the following:

/* Desktop: show full icon names over several lines instead of cutting
   them to one line with "..." */
XfdesktopIconView.view { -XfdesktopIconView-ellipsize-icon-labels: 0; }
